==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From Common Germanic ''*leugan''. Cognates with Old English ''[[leogan|lēoġan]]'' (Modern English ''[[lie]]''), Old Saxon ''[[liogan]]'' (Dutch ''[[liegen]]''), Old High German ''[[liogan]]'' (German ''[[lügen]]''), Gothic '''[[𐌻𐌹𐌿𐌲𐌰𐌽]]'''. Ultimately from Proto-Indo-European ''*leugh-''. Indo-European cognates include Lithuanian ''[[lūgoti]]''.

===Verb===
'''ljúga'''

# to [[lie]], to tell [[lies]]

